@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-construction`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-repeals`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-general`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-eu`

-- The Interpretation Act 1978 (1978 c. 30): assimilated direct legislation (s 23ZA), Acts of the Scottish Parliament (s 23A), Welsh legislation
-- (ss 23B and 23C) and Northern Ireland (s 24).
--
-- Source: the converter-made plain-text rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1978-30.txt, not the official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- WHAT THE SECTIONS TURN ON. They turn on Acts that are not among the sources (the Scotland Act 1998, the Government of Wales Act 2006, the Legislation
-- (Wales) Act 2019, the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, the Fisheries Act 2020, the Northern Ireland Acts) and on days the text refers to without giving
-- ("exit day", "IP completion day"). A fact that comes from one of those is an INPUT, a boolean the caller sets or a day the caller gives; a meaning that one of
-- those Acts supplies ("devolved Welsh authority", "Welsh zone", "Wales") is asked as an input and returned. Where the caller gives none, the function refuses by name.
-- Whether a provision applies "so far as applicable" to a particular instrument is not settled here (fork F19).
--
-- A boolean named "... counts ..." answers TRUE when the section says so and FALSE when it does not say so; FALSE never means the opposite is the law.
-- An answer `does not apply` of the type `Extent of application` means that the section applies nothing there, not that nothing else does.

§ `Nouns of this module`

-- The kinds of legislation that section 23ZA(6) lists as devolution legislation, with the kinds that are not.
DECLARE `A kind of legislation named in section 23ZA(6)` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `Northern Ireland legislation`
    `an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `an instrument made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `an instrument made under Northern Ireland legislation`
    `an Act of Parliament`
    `assimilated direct legislation`
    `other legislation`

DECLARE `What the second reference to an Act in section 11 may be` IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `assimilated direct legislation so far as amended`
    `assimilated direct legislation so far as unamended`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Scottish legislation` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament`

DECLARE `A Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` IS ONE OF
    `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales`

DECLARE `Legislation that section 23C names` IS ONE OF
    `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `an instrument made under such a Measure or Act`
    `an instrument made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation`
    `other legislation`

DECLARE `Expression that section 23B(6) takes from the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS ONE OF
    `devolved Welsh authority`
    `Welsh zone`
    `Wales`

DECLARE `Kind of Northern Ireland legislation` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Parliament of Ireland`
    `an Act of the Parliament of Northern Ireland`
    `an Order in Council under section 1(3) of the Northern Ireland (Temporary Provisions) Act 1972`
    `a Measure of the Northern Ireland Assembly established under section 1 of the Northern Ireland Assembly Act 1973`
    `an Order in Council under Schedule 1 to the Northern Ireland Act 1974`
    `an Act of the Northern Ireland Assembly`
    `an Order in Council under section 85 of the Northern Ireland Act 1998`
    `another kind of legislation`

DECLARE `Definition named in section 24(4)` IS ONE OF
    `The Communities`
    `The Corporation Tax Acts`
    `E.C.S.C. Treaty`
    `E.E.C. Treaty`
    `EEA agreement and EEA state`
    `Entry date`
    `The EU or the European Union`
    `EU institution`
    `EU instrument`
    `Euratom, Economic Community and Coal and Steel Community`
    `Euratom Treaty`
    `European Court`
    `The Income Tax Acts`
    `Member (in the expression "member State")`
    `The Tax Acts`
    `The Treaties or the EU Treaties`
    `another definition of Schedule 1`

§ `Named refusals of this module`

-- A refusal is an expression at any type; each name is its message.

-- src:158 | (6) In this section, “devolved Welsh authority” , “Welsh zone” and (subject to subsection (7)) “Wales” have the same meanings as in the Government of Wales Act 2006 (see sections 157A and 158 of that Act).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(6) (src:158): the meanings are those of the Government of Wales Act 2006, which is not among the sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 23B(6) takes the meaning from the Government of Wales Act 2006, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 23B(6) takes the meaning from the Government of Wales Act 2006, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it"

§ `Section 23ZA: assimilated direct legislation`

-- "(1) The provisions of this Act (except sections 1 to 4, 13 and 19(2)) apply, so far as applicable and unless the contrary intention appears, to any assimilated direct
-- legislation so far as it (a) is amended by an Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation, and (b) is not subordinate legislation, as they apply to an Act
-- passed at the corresponding time."
-- src:111 | 23ZA Assimilated direct legislation
-- src:112 | (1) The provisions of this Act (except sections 1 to 4, 13 and 19(2)) apply, so far as applicable and unless the contrary intention appears, to any assimilated direct legislation so far as it—
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(1) (src:111-112): "except sections 1 to 4, 13 and 19(2)"
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(1) excepts the provision` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `section 1`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 2`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 3`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 4(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 4(b)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 13`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 19(2)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:111 | 23ZA Assimilated direct legislation
-- src:112 | (1) The provisions of this Act (except sections 1 to 4, 13 and 19(2)) apply, so far as applicable and unless the contrary intention appears, to any assimilated direct legislation so far as it—
-- src:113 | (a) is amended by an Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation, and
-- src:114 | (b) is not subordinate legislation,
-- src:115 | as they apply to an Act passed at the corresponding time.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(1) (src:111-115)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      `the corresponding time` IS A DATE
      `it is amended by an Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 23ZA(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to assimilated direct legislation` provision `the corresponding time` `it is amended by an Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation` `it is subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `it is amended by an Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation`)
         OR `it is subordinate legislation`
         OR (`section 23ZA(1) excepts the provision` provision)
    THEN `does not apply`
    ELSE `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision `the corresponding time`

-- "(2) In their application by virtue of subsection (1) (a) section 10 has effect as if the reference to the passing of the Act were a reference to the corresponding time"
-- src:116 | (2) In their application by virtue of subsection (1)—
-- src:117 | (a) section 10 has effect as if the reference to the passing of the Act were a reference to the corresponding time,
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(2)(a) (src:116-117)
GIVEN `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the corresponding time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which Sovereign`
`section 23ZA(2)(a) — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the corresponding time` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    `section 10 — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the corresponding time` `the contrary intention appears`

-- "(b) section 11 has effect as if the second reference to an Act included a reference to the assimilated direct legislation so far as unamended (as well as ... so far as amended)"
-- src:116 | (2) In their application by virtue of subsection (1)—
-- src:118 | (b) section 11 has effect as if the second reference to an Act included a reference to the assimilated direct legislation so far as unamended (as well as a reference to that legislation so far as amended), and
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(2)(b) (src:116) and (src:118)
GIVEN thing IS A `What the second reference to an Act in section 11 may be`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(2)(b) counts the thing as the Act in the second reference of section 11` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `assimilated direct legislation so far as amended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `assimilated direct legislation so far as unamended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

-- "(c) section 16(1) has effect as if the reference to the repealing Act not being passed were a reference to the repeal not having been made"
-- src:116 | (2) In their application by virtue of subsection (1)—
-- src:119 | (c) section 16(1) has effect as if the reference to the repealing Act not being passed were a reference to the repeal not having been made.
-- src:69 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the repealing Act had not been passed.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(2)(c) (src:116) and (src:119), with s 16(1), closing words (src:69)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that section 16(1) protects`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(2)(c) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repeal had not been made` thing `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` thing `the contrary intention appears`

-- "(3) References in this Act to the repeal of an enactment are to be read, in the case of an enactment which is assimilated direct legislation, as references to the revocation of the enactment."
-- src:120 | (3) References in this Act to the repeal of an enactment are to be read, in the case of an enactment which is assimilated direct legislation, as references to the revocation of the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(3) (src:120)
GIVEN `the enactment is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Name the Act gives to an event`
`section 23ZA(3) names the repeal of the enactment as` `the enactment is assimilated direct legislation` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment is assimilated direct legislation`
    THEN `revocation`
    ELSE `repeal`

-- "(4) In Schedule 1 (a) in the definition of "Commencement", the references to an enactment do not include any assimilated direct legislation other than (i) any such legislation to which
-- subsection (1) applies, ... (ia) any instrument made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation ..., or (ii) any instrument, not falling within sub-paragraph (ia),
-- made on or after IP completion day under any assimilated direct legislation". "exit day" and "IP completion day" are inputs. (ii) is read literally: an instrument that is
-- under CAP legislation but made before exit day is not within (ia), and is within (ii) only if it was made on or after IP completion day (the days given, in the order the Act has
-- them, make that the same thing as being made after exit day, but the function does not rely on the order).
-- src:121 | (4) In Schedule 1—
-- src:122 | (a) in the definition of “Commencement”, the references to an enactment do not include any assimilated direct legislation other than—
-- src:123 | (i) any such legislation to which subsection (1) applies, ...
-- src:124 | (ia) any instrument made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020, or
-- src:125 | (ii) any instrument , not falling within sub-paragraph (ia), made on or after IP completion day under any assimilated direct legislation, and
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(4)(a) (src:121-125)
GIVEN `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `exit day` IS A DATE
      `IP completion day` IS A DATE
      `section 23ZA(1) applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument made under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument made under any assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(4)(a) counts the assimilated direct legislation as an enactment in the definition of Commencement` `the day it was made` `exit day` `IP completion day` `section 23ZA(1) applies to it` `it is an instrument made under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020` `it is an instrument made under any assimilated direct legislation` MEANS
    LET `it is within paragraph (ia)` BE
        `it is an instrument made under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020` AND `the day it was made` AT LEAST `exit day`
    IN     `section 23ZA(1) applies to it`
        OR `it is within paragraph (ia)`
        OR (`it is an instrument made under any assimilated direct legislation` AND (NOT `it is within paragraph (ia)`) AND `the day it was made` AT LEAST `IP completion day`)

-- src:121 | (4) In Schedule 1—
-- src:126 | (b) in the definitions of “The Corporation Tax Acts” and “The Income Tax Acts”, the references to an enactment do not include any assimilated direct legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(4)(b) (src:121) and (src:126)
GIVEN `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(4)(b) counts the thing as an enactment in the definition of the Corporation Tax Acts or the Income Tax Acts` `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` `it is assimilated direct legislation` MEANS
    `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` AND (NOT `it is assimilated direct legislation`)

-- "(5) For the application of this Act to assimilated direct legislation which is subordinate legislation, see section 23(1) and (2)."
-- src:127 | (5) For the application of this Act to assimilated direct legislation which is subordinate legislation, see section 23(1) and (2).
-- src:107 | (1) The provisions of this Act, except sections 1 to 3 and 4(b), apply, so far as applicable and unless the contrary intention appears, to subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act and, to the extent specified in Part II of Schedule 2, to subordinate legislation made before the commencement of this Act, as they apply to Acts.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(5) (src:127), with s 23(1) (src:107)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
      `it is an Order in Council that section 23(4) names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 23ZA(5) — the extent to which the provision applies to assimilated direct legislation that is subordinate legislation made on` provision day `it is an Order in Council that section 23(4) names` MEANS
    `the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made on` provision day `it is an Order in Council that section 23(4) names`

-- "(6) In this section "corresponding time" means the time when the amending Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation was passed or (as the case may be) made"
-- src:128 | (6) In this section—
-- src:129 | “corresponding time” means the time when the amending Act, subordinate legislation or devolution legislation was passed or (as the case may be) made, and
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(6) (src:128-129)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
GIVETH A DATE
`section 23ZA(6) — the corresponding time` e MEANS
    e's `the day it was passed or made`

-- ""devolution legislation" means (a) an Act of the Scottish Parliament, (b) a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales, (c) Northern Ireland legislation ..., or (d) an instrument made under anything falling within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)."
-- src:128 | (6) In this section—
-- src:130 | “devolution legislation” means—
-- src:131 | (a) an Act of the Scottish Parliament,
-- src:132 | (b) a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales,
-- src:133 | (c) Northern Ireland legislation (for the meaning of which see section 24(5)), or
-- src:134 | (d) an instrument made under anything falling within paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23ZA(6) (src:128) and (src:130-134)
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of legislation named in section 23ZA(6)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23ZA(6) counts the legislation as devolution legislation` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument made under Northern Ireland legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of Parliament` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `assimilated direct legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `other legislation` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 23A: Acts of the Scottish Parliament`

-- "(1) This Act applies in relation to an Act of the Scottish Parliament and an instrument made under such an Act only to the extent provided in this section.
-- (2) Except as provided in subsection (3) below, sections 15 to 18 apply to (a) an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to an Act, (b) an instrument made under
-- an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to subordinate legislation."
-- src:135 | 23A Acts of the Scottish Parliament etc.
-- src:136 | (1) This Act applies in relation to an Act of the Scottish Parliament and an instrument made under such an Act only to the extent provided in this section.
-- src:137 | (2) Except as provided in subsection (3) below, sections 15 to 18 apply to—
-- src:138 | (a) an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to an Act,
-- src:139 | (b) an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to subordinate legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23A(1) and (2) (src:135-139)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23A(2) names the provision among sections 15 to 18` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `section 15`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 16(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 16(2)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 17(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 17(2)(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 17(2)(b)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 18`    THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:135 | 23A Acts of the Scottish Parliament etc.
-- src:136 | (1) This Act applies in relation to an Act of the Scottish Parliament and an instrument made under such an Act only to the extent provided in this section.
-- src:137 | (2) Except as provided in subsection (3) below, sections 15 to 18 apply to—
-- src:138 | (a) an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to an Act,
-- src:139 | (b) an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament as they apply to subordinate legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23A(1) and (2) (src:135-139)
GIVEN kind      IS A `Scottish legislation`
      provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 23A — the extent to which the provision applies to the Scottish legislation passed or made on` kind provision day MEANS
    IF   NOT (`section 23A(2) names the provision among sections 15 to 18` provision)
    THEN `does not apply`
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision day
         WHEN `an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN `the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made on` provision day FALSE

-- "(3) In the application of those sections to an Act and to subordinate legislation (a) references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under,
-- an Act of the Scottish Parliament, and (b) the reference in section 17(2)(b) to subordinate legislation includes an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament."
-- src:140 | (3) In the application of those sections to an Act and to subordinate legislation—
-- src:141 | (a) references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament, and
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23A(3)(a) (src:140-141)
GIVEN `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23A(3)(a) counts the thing as an enactment in sections 15 to 18` `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` MEANS
    `it is an enactment apart from this paragraph` OR `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament`

-- src:140 | (3) In the application of those sections to an Act and to subordinate legislation—
-- src:142 | (b) the reference in section 17(2)(b) to subordinate legislation includes an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23A(3)(b) (src:140) and (src:142)
GIVEN `it is subordinate legislation apart from this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23A(3)(b) counts the instrument as subordinate legislation in section 17(2)(b)` `it is subordinate legislation apart from this paragraph` `it is an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` MEANS
    `it is subordinate legislation apart from this paragraph` OR `it is an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament`

-- "(4) In the application of section 20 to an Act and to subordinate legislation, references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament."
-- src:143 | (4) In the application of section 20 to an Act and to subordinate legislation, references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23A(4) (src:143)
GIVEN `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23A(4) counts the thing as an enactment in section 20` `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` MEANS
    `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` OR `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament`

§ `Section 23B: Welsh legislation`

-- "(1) The provisions of this Act, except sections 1 to 3, apply to the following as they apply to an Act (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales, and (b) an Act of the National
-- Assembly for Wales, other than the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019, which receives Royal Assent before 1 January 2020". "before 1 January 2020" is a date: an Act that receives Royal Assent
-- on that day is not before it. A Measure or Act that this subsection does not reach gets `does not apply` from it; the Act does not say here what reaches it.
-- src:145 | (1) The provisions of this Act, except sections 1 to 3, apply to the following as they apply to an Act—
-- src:146 | (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales, and
-- src:147 | (b) an Act of the National Assembly for Wales, other than the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019, which receives Royal Assent before 1 January 2020 (the day on which Part 2 of that Act comes fully into force).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(1) (src:145-147)
GIVEN kind      IS A `A Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
      `it is the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 23B(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to a Measure or Act enacted on` kind `it is the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019` provision day MEANS
    LET reached BE
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN (NOT `it is the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019`) AND day LESS THAN (YMD 2020 1 1)
    IN   IF   (NOT reached) OR (`section 23B(1) excepts the provision` provision)
         THEN `does not apply`
         ELSE `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision day

-- src:145 | (1) The provisions of this Act, except sections 1 to 3, apply to the following as they apply to an Act—
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(1) (src:145): "except sections 1 to 3"
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23B(1) excepts the provision` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `section 1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 3` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "(2) The provisions of this Act apply to an instrument (a) made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales, and (b) made before 1 January 2020, as they apply to other subordinate legislation."
-- src:148 | (2) The provisions of this Act apply to an instrument—
-- src:149 | (a) made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales, and
-- src:150 | (b) made before 1 January 2020,
-- src:151 | as they apply to other subordinate legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(2) (src:148-151)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
      `it is made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 23B(2) — the extent to which the provision applies to an instrument made on` provision day `it is made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` MEANS
    IF   `it is made under a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` AND day LESS THAN (YMD 2020 1 1)
    THEN `the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made on` provision day FALSE
    ELSE `does not apply`

-- "(3) The provisions of this Act apply to an instrument made under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation, and made by the Welsh Ministers or any other devolved Welsh authority,
-- only if (a) the instrument is made before 1 January 2020, (b) the instrument is made (at any time) with any other person who is not a devolved Welsh authority, or (c) the instrument contains
-- any provision that applies otherwise than in relation to Wales." An instrument that the subsection does not describe is not barred by it.
-- src:152 | (3) The provisions of this Act apply to an instrument made under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation, and made by the Welsh Ministers or any other devolved Welsh authority, only if—
-- src:153 | (a) the instrument is made before 1 January 2020,
-- src:154 | (b) the instrument is made (at any time) with any other person who is not a devolved Welsh authority, or
-- src:155 | (c) the instrument contains any provision that applies otherwise than in relation to Wales.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(3) (src:152-155)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `it is made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made with a person who is not a devolved Welsh authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains a provision that applies otherwise than in relation to Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23B(3) allows the provisions of the Act to apply to the instrument made on` day `it is made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation` `it is made with a person who is not a devolved Welsh authority` `it contains a provision that applies otherwise than in relation to Wales` MEANS
        NOT `it is made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation`
    OR  day LESS THAN (YMD 2020 1 1)
    OR  `it is made with a person who is not a devolved Welsh authority`
    OR  `it contains a provision that applies otherwise than in relation to Wales`

-- "(4) Nothing in subsection (2) or (3) limits the operation of sections 12 to 14A in relation to a power or duty to make an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies,
-- but section 11 does not apply in relation to such an instrument."
-- src:156 | (4) Nothing in subsection (2) or (3) limits the operation of sections 12 to 14A in relation to a power or duty to make an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies, but section 11 does not apply in relation to such an instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(4) (src:156): "sections 12 to 14A"
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23B(4) provides that subsections (2) and (3) do not limit the operation of the provision` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `section 12` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 13` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 14` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 14A` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:156 | (4) Nothing in subsection (2) or (3) limits the operation of sections 12 to 14A in relation to a power or duty to make an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies, but section 11 does not apply in relation to such an instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(4) (src:156): "section 11 does not apply in relation to such an instrument"
GIVEN `it is an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23B(4) provides that section 11 does not apply in relation to the instrument` `it is an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies` MEANS
    `it is an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies`

-- "(5) In the application of this Act to a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales, references to the passing of an Act or an enactment are to be read as references to the enactment of the Measure or Act."
-- src:157 | (5) In the application of this Act to a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales, references to the passing of an Act or an enactment are to be read as references to the enactment of the Measure or Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(5) (src:157)
GIVEN `it is a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Name the Act gives to an event`
`section 23B(5) names the passing of the Act or enactment as` `it is a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` MEANS
    IF   `it is a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    THEN `enactment of the Measure or Act`
    ELSE `passing`

-- "(6) In this section, "devolved Welsh authority", "Welsh zone" and (subject to subsection (7)) "Wales" have the same meanings as in the Government of Wales Act 2006 (see sections 157A and 158 of that Act)."
-- src:158 | (6) In this section, “devolved Welsh authority” , “Welsh zone” and (subject to subsection (7)) “Wales” have the same meanings as in the Government of Wales Act 2006 (see sections 157A and 158 of that Act).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(6) (src:158)
GIVEN expression IS AN `Expression that section 23B(6) takes from the Government of Wales Act 2006`
      `the meaning it has in the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`section 23B(6) — the meaning of the expression` expression `the meaning it has in the Government of Wales Act 2006` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the meaning it has in the Government of Wales Act 2006`
    WHEN JUST meaning THEN meaning
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 23B(6) takes the meaning from the Government of Wales Act 2006, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it`

-- "(7) In relation to a provision that (a) relates to fishing, fisheries or fish health, and (b) is contained in an instrument made after section 45 of the Fisheries Act 2020 comes into force,
-- "Wales" includes the area of the Welsh zone beyond the seaward limit of the territorial sea." A section comes into force at the beginning of its day (s 4), so an instrument made on that day is made after it.
-- src:159 | (7) In relation to a provision that—
-- src:160 | (a) relates to fishing, fisheries or fish health, and
-- src:161 | (b) is contained in an instrument made after section 45 of the Fisheries Act 2020 comes into force,
-- src:162 | “Wales” includes the area of the Welsh zone beyond the seaward limit of the territorial sea.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23B(7) (src:159-162)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was made` IS A DATE
      `the day section 45 of the Fisheries Act 2020 came into force` IS A DATE
      `the provision relates to fishing, fisheries or fish health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23B(7) includes in Wales the area of the Welsh zone beyond the seaward limit of the territorial sea` `the day the instrument was made` `the day section 45 of the Fisheries Act 2020 came into force` `the provision relates to fishing, fisheries or fish health` MEANS
        `the provision relates to fishing, fisheries or fish health`
    AND `the day the instrument was made` AT LEAST `the day section 45 of the Fisheries Act 2020 came into force`

§ `Section 23C: interpretation of this Act in relation to Welsh legislation`

-- "(1) In this Act, references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales, (b) an Act of the National Assembly for Wales (whenever the Act receives
-- Royal Assent), (c) an instrument made under such an Act or Measure (whenever the instrument is made), or (d) an instrument made under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation, and made by
-- the Welsh Ministers or any other devolved Welsh authority (whenever the instrument is made, and whether or not it is made with any other person), but the reference in section 16(2) to a temporary
-- enactment does not include an enactment comprised in legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies."
-- src:163 | 23C Interpretation of this Act in relation to Welsh legislation
-- src:164 | (1) In this Act, references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in—
-- src:165 | (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales,
-- src:166 | (b) an Act of the National Assembly for Wales (whenever the Act receives Royal Assent),
-- src:167 | (c) an instrument made under such an Act or Measure (whenever the instrument is made), or
-- src:168 | (d) an instrument made under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation, and made by the Welsh Ministers or any other devolved Welsh authority (whenever the instrument is made, and whether or not it is made with any other person),
-- src:169 | but the reference in section 16(2) to a temporary enactment does not include an enactment comprised in legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies (see section 3(1) of that Act).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23C(1) (src:163-169)
GIVEN kind IS A `Legislation that section 23C names`
      `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the reference in section 16(2) to a temporary enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23C(1) counts an enactment comprised in the legislation as an enactment` kind `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it` `it is the reference in section 16(2) to a temporary enactment` MEANS
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an instrument made under such a Measure or Act` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an instrument made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `other legislation` THEN FALSE)
    AND (NOT (`it is the reference in section 16(2) to a temporary enactment` AND `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it`))

-- "(1A) In section 14(b), the reference to a statutory instrument includes a Welsh statutory instrument."
-- src:170 | (1A) In section 14(b), the reference to a statutory instrument includes a Welsh statutory instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23C(1A) (src:170)
GIVEN `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Welsh statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23C(1A) counts the instrument as a statutory instrument in section 14(b)` `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` `it is a Welsh statutory instrument` MEANS
    `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` OR `it is a Welsh statutory instrument`

-- "(2) In section 17(2)(b), the reference to subordinate legislation includes an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies."
-- src:171 | (2) In section 17(2)(b), the reference to subordinate legislation includes an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23C(2) (src:171)
GIVEN `it is subordinate legislation apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23C(2) counts the instrument as subordinate legislation in section 17(2)(b)` `it is subordinate legislation apart from this subsection` `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it` MEANS
    `it is subordinate legislation apart from this subsection` OR `Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies to it`

-- "(3) In section 18, the reference to an act or omission which constitutes an offence under two or more Acts includes an act or omission which constitutes an offence under (a) any legislation to which
-- that section applies, and (b) any legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies, and the reference to "those Acts" is to be read accordingly."
-- "and" between (a) and (b) is read as it stands: the act or omission is an offence under legislation of both kinds (fork F27).
-- src:172 | (3) In section 18, the reference to an act or omission which constitutes an offence under two or more Acts includes an act or omission which constitutes an offence under—
-- src:173 | (a) any legislation to which that section applies, and
-- src:174 | (b) any legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies,
-- src:175 | and the reference to “those Acts” is to be read accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23C(3) (src:172-175)
GIVEN `it constitutes an offence under two or more Acts apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it constitutes an offence under legislation to which section 18 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it constitutes an offence under legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23C(3) counts the act or omission as constituting an offence under two or more Acts in section 18` `it constitutes an offence under two or more Acts apart from this subsection` `it constitutes an offence under legislation to which section 18 applies` `it constitutes an offence under legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies` MEANS
        `it constitutes an offence under two or more Acts apart from this subsection`
    OR (`it constitutes an offence under legislation to which section 18 applies` AND `it constitutes an offence under legislation to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies`)

-- "(4) In section 19(1), references to "another Act" include (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales, and (b) an Act of the National Assembly for Wales (whenever the Act receives Royal Assent)"
-- src:176 | (4) In section 19(1), references to “another Act” include—
-- src:177 | (a) a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales, and
-- src:178 | (b) an Act of the National Assembly for Wales (whenever the Act receives Royal Assent),
-- src:179 | and the reference in paragraph (c) to “Acts” is to be read accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23C(4) (src:176-179)
GIVEN `it is another Act apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Legislation that section 23C names`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23C(4) counts the legislation as another Act in section 19(1)` `it is another Act apart from this subsection` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument made under such a Measure or Act` THEN `it is another Act apart from this subsection`
    WHEN `an instrument made by the Welsh Ministers or another devolved Welsh authority under an Act of Parliament or assimilated direct legislation` THEN `it is another Act apart from this subsection`
    WHEN `other legislation` THEN `it is another Act apart from this subsection`

§ `Section 24: Northern Ireland`

-- "(1) This Act extends to Northern Ireland so far as it applies to Acts or subordinate legislation which so extend."
-- src:180 | 24 Application to Northern Ireland.
-- src:181 | (1) This Act extends to Northern Ireland so far as it applies to Acts or subordinate legislation which so extend.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(1) (src:180-181)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
      `the Act or subordinate legislation extends to Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 24(1) — the extent to which the provision extends to Northern Ireland for an Act passed on` provision day `the Act or subordinate legislation extends to Northern Ireland` MEANS
    IF   `the Act or subordinate legislation extends to Northern Ireland`
    THEN `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision day
    ELSE `does not apply`

-- "(2) In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in Northern Ireland
-- legislation whenever passed or made; and in relation to such legislation references to the passing or repeal of an enactment include the making or revocation of an Order in Council."
-- src:182 | (2) In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in Northern Ireland legislation whenever passed or made; and in relation to such legislation references to the passing or repeal of an enactment include the making or revocation of an Order in Council.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(2) (src:182): the first limb
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is comprised in Northern Ireland legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 24(2) counts the thing as an enactment` e `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` `it is comprised in Northern Ireland legislation` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
    THEN `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` OR `it is comprised in Northern Ireland legislation`
    ELSE `it is an enactment apart from this subsection`

-- src:182 | (2) In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in Northern Ireland legislation whenever passed or made; and in relation to such legislation references to the passing or repeal of an enactment include the making or revocation of an Order in Council.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(2) (src:182): the second limb
GIVEN e     IS AN `An enactment`
      event IS AN `Event in the life of an enactment`
      name  IS A `Name the Act gives to an event`
      `it is an Order in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 24(2) counts the name as the event for an enactment comprised in Northern Ireland legislation` e event name `it is an Order in Council` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`))
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER event
         WHEN `its passing` THEN name EQUALS `passing` OR (`it is an Order in Council` AND name EQUALS `making`)
         WHEN `its repeal`  THEN name EQUALS `repeal` OR (`it is an Order in Council` AND name EQUALS `revocation`)

-- "(3) In the application of section 14 to Acts passed after the commencement of this Act which extend to Northern Ireland, "statutory instrument" includes statutory rule for the purposes of the Statutory Rules (Northern Ireland) Order 1979."
-- src:183 | (3) In the application of section 14 to Acts passed after the commencement of this Act which extend to Northern Ireland, “statutory instrument” includes statutory rule for the purposes of the Statutory Rules (Northern Ireland) Order 1979.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(3) (src:183)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      `the Act extends to Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statutory rule for the purposes of the Statutory Rules (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 24(3) counts the thing as a statutory instrument in section 14` e `the Act extends to Northern Ireland` `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` `it is a statutory rule for the purposes of the Statutory Rules (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
         AND `the Act extends to Northern Ireland`
         AND (e's `its kind`) EQUALS `an Act`
    THEN `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection` OR `it is a statutory rule for the purposes of the Statutory Rules (Northern Ireland) Order 1979`
    ELSE `it is a statutory instrument apart from this subsection`

-- "(3A) Section 20A applies to Northern Ireland legislation as it applies to Acts."
-- src:184 | (3A) Section 20A applies to Northern Ireland legislation as it applies to Acts.
-- src:96 | 20A References to certain EU instruments
-- src:97 | Where an Act passed after the commencement of this section refers to a EU instrument that has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument, the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to that instrument as so amended, extended or applied.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(3A) (src:184), with s 20A (src:96-97)
GIVEN `it is Northern Ireland legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      `the day section 20A came into force` IS A DATE
      `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How a reference is read`
`section 24(3A) applies section 20A to the Northern Ireland legislation` `it is Northern Ireland legislation` day `the day section 20A came into force` `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` `it is assimilated direct legislation` `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `it is Northern Ireland legislation`
    THEN `section 20A — how the reference is read` day `the day section 20A came into force` `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` `it is assimilated direct legislation` `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument` `the contrary intention appears`
    ELSE `no reading is given by this provision`

-- "(4) The following definitions contained in Schedule 1, namely those of [seventeen rows, the first blank and the second with its dots] apply, unless the contrary intention appears, to Northern Ireland legislation as they apply to Acts."
-- src:185 | (4) The following definitions contained in Schedule 1, namely those of—
-- src:187 | The Communities ...;
-- src:188 | The Corporation Tax Acts;
-- src:189 | E.C.S.C. Treaty;
-- src:190 | E.E.C. Treaty;
-- src:191 | EEA agreement and EEA state;
-- src:192 | Entry date;
-- src:193 | The EU or the European Union;
-- src:194 | EU institution;
-- src:195 | EU instrument;
-- src:196 | Euratom, Economic Community and Coal and Steel Community;
-- src:197 | Euratom Treaty;
-- src:198 | European Court;
-- src:199 | The Income Tax Acts;
-- src:200 | Member (in the expression “member State”);
-- src:201 | The Tax Acts ;
-- src:202 | The Treaties or the EU Treaties,
-- src:203 | apply, unless the contrary intention appears, to Northern Ireland legislation as they apply to Acts.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(4) (src:185-203)
GIVEN definition IS A `Definition named in section 24(4)`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 24(4) applies the Schedule 1 definition to Northern Ireland legislation` definition `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `the contrary intention appears`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER definition
         WHEN `The Communities` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `The Corporation Tax Acts` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `E.C.S.C. Treaty` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `E.E.C. Treaty` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `EEA agreement and EEA state` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `Entry date` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `The EU or the European Union` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `EU institution` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `EU instrument` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `Euratom, Economic Community and Coal and Steel Community` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `Euratom Treaty` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `European Court` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `The Income Tax Acts` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `Member (in the expression "member State")` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `The Tax Acts` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `The Treaties or the EU Treaties` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `another definition of Schedule 1` THEN FALSE

-- "(5) In this section "Northern Ireland legislation" means (a) to (g)".
-- src:204 | (5) In this section “Northern Ireland legislation” means—
-- src:205 | (a) Acts of the Parliament of Ireland;
-- src:206 | (b) Acts of the Parliament of Northern Ireland;
-- src:207 | (c) Orders in Council under section 1(3) of the Northern Ireland (Temporary Provisions) Act 1972;
-- src:208 | (d) Measures of the Northern Ireland Assembly established under section 1 of the Northern Ireland Assembly Act 1973;
-- src:209 | (e) Orders in Council under Schedule 1 to the Northern Ireland Act 1974;
-- src:210 | (f) Acts of the Northern Ireland Assembly; and
-- src:211 | (g) Orders in Council under section 85 of the Northern Ireland Act 1998.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 24(5) (src:204-211)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Northern Ireland legislation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 24(5) counts the legislation as Northern Ireland legislation` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act of the Parliament of Ireland` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the Parliament of Northern Ireland` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Order in Council under section 1(3) of the Northern Ireland (Temporary Provisions) Act 1972` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Measure of the Northern Ireland Assembly established under section 1 of the Northern Ireland Assembly Act 1973` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Order in Council under Schedule 1 to the Northern Ireland Act 1974` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the Northern Ireland Assembly` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Order in Council under section 85 of the Northern Ireland Act 1998` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of legislation` THEN FALSE
